    [Doc][Misc] Update GLM-5.3-Flash deployment and evaluation guide (#18276)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update the GLM-5.3-Flash deployment guide for vLLM-Ascend v0.30.0RC1.
    Atlas 800I A3 PD deployment uses DP2/TP8 Prefill and DP8/TP2 Decode,
    with matching HCCS settings, Decode graph mode, MTP options, int8 KV
    cache, launcher ports, and proxy endpoints. Use canonical CLI option
    names throughout the examples.
    
    Configure the Atlas 800I A3 KV Cache Pool with the preinstalled Memcache
    backend and DDR memory. Prefill and Decode each allocate 20GB per
    worker: 16 workers per node contribute 320GB each, for a 640GB pool.
    Include MetaService configuration, prefix-caching overrides, and
    connector settings. Keep Atlas 800I A2 on Mooncake with self-contained
    configuration examples, and correct Atlas 800I A2 device counts and
    distributed startup/readiness instructions.
    
    Refresh the container image tags and Atlas 800I A3 single-node
    parameters. Mount /etc/hccn.conf read-only in the Atlas 800I A3
    containers on both nodes. Add Atlas 800I A3 PD accuracy results for GPQA
    (89.9; max_tokens=131072) and MMMU-PRO (78.4; max_tokens=98304), both
    using temperature=1.0 and top_p=0.95.
    
    Use the main-branch KV Cache Pool guide path and hardware compatibility
    anchor. The equivalent releases/v0.30.0 update is #18275. This PR
    contains one signed-off commit.
    
    Synchronize the Chinese `.po` with the English guide: translate all 157
    current entries, remove 11 obsolete entries, and adapt section links to
    the generated Chinese pages.
    
    Set the English and Chinese navigation titles to `GLM-5.3-Flash`,
    matching the page heading.
    
    Group the two PD deployment scenarios in Sections 5.3 and 5.4 after the
    multi-node colocated example in Section 5.2. Move PD accuracy results to
    Section 7.2, add model-specific performance tuning in Section 9, and
    update hardware names. Omit explicit Prefill compilation settings;
    retain Decode graph mode and MTP settings. Clarify MTP draft graph
    support and the image limit through the PD proxy. Move the model support
    entries into the multimodal tables, with supported Atlas 800I A2 and
    Atlas 800I A3 deployment and experimental 950DT Products deployment.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation and deployment examples only; no runtime code changes.
    Atlas 800I A2 and Atlas 800I A3 support is documented for v0.30.0RC1,
    while 950DT Products support remains experimental.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Chinese PO has 100% translation coverage and compiles to a gettext
    catalog. Generated the Chinese page and verified exact fenced code,
    inline parameters, tabs/lists/tables, relevant section links, DDR
    sizing, and accuracy results against English.
    - Verified that the navigation hook sets `GLM-5.3-Flash` for both
    DOCS_LANG=en and DOCS_LANG=zh; Ruff check and format passed.
    - Markdownlint, codespell, typos, and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Rechecked all 157 Chinese entries, Jinja parsing, section anchors,
    rendered structure, and unchanged serving examples after reordering; all
    34 Shell/Python examples passed syntax checks. Exercised the current
    capture-size adjustment and Atlas 800I A3 fused-MC2 selector without NPU
    imports.
    - Validated all 33 Shell examples with `bash -n`, parsed the Python
    example, and parsed embedded JSON/INI settings.
    - Expanded and parsed all four MultiConnector fragments across DP ranks,
    checked unique engine IDs and lookup ports, and verified local
    documentation links.
    - Verified the 20GB-per-worker DDR configuration and total pool
    capacity. Verified explicit Prefill graph settings and Decode
    enable_static_kernel settings were removed; Decode graph mode and MTP
    settings are retained.
    - `bash format.sh ci` was attempted but stopped while installing
    actionlint's Go environment on Windows: `ValueError: Could not find a
    version matching your system requirements (os=windows; arch=)`. The full
    hook suite did not run.
    - Accuracy results were recorded from existing Atlas 800I A3 PD testing;
    NPU inference and evaluation were not rerun locally for this
    documentation change.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    Signed-off-by: YanpengDing <dingyanpeng18@163.com>

